I've just compiled nethack 3.1.2 for Linux.
My 15th-level barbarian was wandering around looking for a bag of
holding to put all his artifacts in, when "Suddenly, the dungeon
collapses".  After a bit of investigation I discovered that the cause
of the problem was that I'd run out of disk space :-(.

Not to worry, I thought, I've compiled the game with INSURANCE, and I'd
been running with the "checkpoint" option set, so I should be able to
make some disk space somehow and recover.  After a quick 'rm -rf
/usr/spool/news/*' I had got some disk space back again. I compiled
recover, and then (after making a copy of the playground), I did a
'recover alock', which executed without complaint. OK, so I ran nethack
to restore the saved game, but after chugging away for a while it tells
me "error restoring saved game"...  :-( :-( :-(

Any suggestions? Is there any way for me to recover my game?
Or is "disk full" a non-recoverable error?
It would be really nice if nethack could handle disk full conditions
a little more gracefully...

